 "notes": "Spine: gap -> Cr-free EHEA + strain sweep -> casting -> L12+B2 lamellar eutectic -> tension -> dislocation evolution at 0.6%, 1.5%, fracture -> two branches: (a) interface pile-up MEC -> strength, and substructure MEC -> three-stage hardening -> hardening capacity -> ductility; (b) interphase voids/cracks -> mixed fracture mode -> conclusion. No PRF node: the paper argues engineering reliability only in one clause. Table 1 (SEM-EDS phase compositions: FCC Fe/Co-rich, B2 Al/Ni-rich) is not in the packet and is left out. Audits: a1 (0.6% TEM shows no resolved pile-up and is post-yield, qualifies the yield-strength pathway), n22 (no phase labels in deformed TEM). Figure-vs-text: F2a failure drop at ~6.5% vs label 6.2%; EBSD area ~70% FCC vs 60% text; TEM lamellae ~0.7-0.9 um vs 1-2 um text.",
 "review": {
  "judge": "senior investigator",
  "verdict": "accept with minor fixes",
  "changes": [
   "e(o3->n6): mm_op register_colocated_views -> inspect_local_feature (o3 reads one TEM panel, F1c; no second view of the same region is registered)",
